WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
Make sure you have a tutor
who has the imagination, the

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.710
wherewithal, the resourcefulness
to keep the conversation going.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:13.260
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here, today
I want to talk about how to get the

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.980
most out of your online language tutor.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.750
Remember if you enjoy these videos,
please subscribe, click on the bell for

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.520
notifications and if you follow me on a
podcast service, please leave a review.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:33.510
So in an earlier video, I said that
I'm gonna work harder on my output.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.320
I'm gonna, you know, work
deliberately with my Persian tutor

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.550
uh, twice a week, we're gonna have
deliberate subjects of conversation.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.270
I'm gonna prepare for them and
we're gonna see how that goes

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.540
over the next three months.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:52.260
I'm particularly looking at how to
effectively use LingQ and the content

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.115
at LingQ and the functionality
at LingQ to integrate that with

00:00:56.324 --> 00:00:57.855
working with an online tutor.

00:00:58.455 --> 00:01:02.415
So this got me to thinking about how to
get the most out of a tutor online tutor.

00:01:02.655 --> 00:01:05.235
Remember there are more
and more online tutors.

00:01:05.504 --> 00:01:07.785
There are online tutors
for every language.

00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:12.315
You can find them at sites like
italkie or verbling, you can find

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.384
them independent, uh, online tutors.

00:01:14.384 --> 00:01:14.955
There are lots.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.770
so it's becoming, if not the
mainstream compared to say language

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:23.580
schools, more and more common
as a way of learning a language.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.679
So how do we benefit the most?

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.050
Obviously we want an online tutor
primarily to have someone to speak

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.570
to, uh, remember that, that the...

00:01:33.574 --> 00:01:35.399
and possibly to explain the grammar.

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:36.869
But to me that's not so important.

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:39.419
I can find lots of
explanations of grammar.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.080
I don't need the teacher to
walk me through the grammar.

00:01:44.415 --> 00:01:48.765
Um, I'm also somewhat skeptical,
skeptical as to how much

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:51.135
benefit there is in corrections.

00:01:51.255 --> 00:01:53.025
It can help, but it's not necessary.

00:01:53.414 --> 00:01:58.664
We do need the tutor for speaking because
eventually to speak well you have to

00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:05.775
speak a lot, but I mean, unless you get
five hours a day with a tutor or even

00:02:05.775 --> 00:02:11.950
three hours a day with a tutor every day,
which can get quite expensive, you know?

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.225
In fact, you have to have a strategy
where you're mixing the tutor in

00:02:15.225 --> 00:02:18.645
with your other activities in order
to come up with something that is

00:02:18.975 --> 00:02:21.045
cost efficient and time efficient.

00:02:21.765 --> 00:02:25.575
Now, I always get back to this idea that
to speak well you have to speak a lot,

00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:28.575
obviously if you're in the country, if
you have friends, if you go out with

00:02:28.575 --> 00:02:31.515
friends or you're working in an office
where everybody speaks the target

00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:36.135
language, that's an ideal scenario and
you're gonna learn to speak more quickly.

00:02:36.405 --> 00:02:41.200
And this was my situation in Japan where
I did a lot of speaking in Japanese,

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.559
but I still did a lot of input.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:44.579
Okay.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.579
And so I think the secret in terms
of working with a tutor is to

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:51.839
mix in the input with the hours
that you spend with the tutor.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:56.910
Quickly some thoughts on, on what
I expect of a tutor, I expect the

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.560
tutor to lead the conversation.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:02:59.640
I don't want...

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.299
and I have had tutors where if
there's a lull in the conversation,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.200
my tutor, most often a female, she's
waiting for me to say something.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.030
I struggle to speak the language.

00:03:09.179 --> 00:03:10.590
I'm not gonna say anything.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.799
The tutor has to keep
the conversation going.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.720
So that's number one, make sure you
have a tutor who has the imagination,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.250
the wherewithal, the resourcefulness
to keep the conversation going when

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.420
there's a love, lull she comes up
with a new subject, a new question,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.100
something to keep the conversation going.

00:03:29.339 --> 00:03:30.420
So I think that's number one.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.239
Number two, make sure you have
a tutor who is encouraging.

00:03:34.859 --> 00:03:38.250
Uh, I have had tutors who make
a face when I make a mistake.

00:03:38.429 --> 00:03:40.049
That's not very good.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.989
You have to wanna get
together with your tutor.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.040
You wanna feel encouraged when you
interact with your tutor, even if

00:03:47.045 --> 00:03:48.899
you haven't improved that much.

00:03:48.929 --> 00:03:52.079
If the tutor tells you you have
improved, that's encouraging.

00:03:52.109 --> 00:03:55.920
So you wanna make sure you have
a tutor who encourages you and

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.480
you enjoy being with that tutor.

00:03:57.929 --> 00:03:58.859
Very, very important.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:06.360
Another thing is I always insist that
my tutor gives me a report with 10 or 15

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.220
words or phrases that I struggled with.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.600
And ideally that...

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:14.130
and they put this in, say, a word
document and ideally, and without any

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.520
English, you know, just the target
language and then they record this.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.910
So that then creates a lesson
for me in LingQ, a lesson that I

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.400
can go back to six months later.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:27.000
All of these conversation reports
become part of a course, which I can

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.770
go back to regularly and review the
words that were important to me at

00:04:31.775 --> 00:04:35.489
a certain stage, which I wanted to
use and maybe didn't use correctly.

00:04:36.539 --> 00:04:41.400
Another thing that we're now starting
to do with my tutor twice a week, which

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.750
is, you know, economical because twice
a week, that's, you know, it costs

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.490
money per hour to be with a tutor.

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:51.645
But she has me focused on specific topics.

00:04:51.885 --> 00:04:53.835
So we are staying with economics.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:57.015
I wanted to move to another
subject and she said, no, we

00:04:57.015 --> 00:04:58.245
wanna stay with economics.

00:04:58.245 --> 00:05:01.125
We're gonna stay with one
subject for a while so that you

00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:02.895
get used to that vocabulary.

00:05:03.105 --> 00:05:09.135
And she then sends me links to
articles in Persian, uh, where I

00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:11.505
come across this kind of vocabulary.

00:05:11.565 --> 00:05:13.035
And so I become familiar with it.

00:05:13.395 --> 00:05:21.450
So here again she is kind of directing
me and keeping me focused from my side.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.600
Because I have two sessions a week
with her, I am motivated to improve.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.950
Uh, most of my learning
at LingQ is, is by myself.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.310
Okay.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:37.020
So I I'm motivated, but when I know that
I'm gonna be discussing economics again

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.100
for the third time in a row with my
tutor, I wanna do better than the last.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.310
So that is quite motivating.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.840
So the tutor not only is an opportunity
for me to, to try to use what I've been,

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:54.330
you know, inputting into my brain, but
I'm also motivated I want to do better.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.410
And if I'm lucky, she'll tell me I
did better, even if it isn't true,

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.240
but all of that contributes to keeping
me going, sending me back with more

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.520
enthusiasm to my input activities.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:11.850
Now, obviously in the final, final
analysis to be a, you know, very

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.030
proficient speaker of Persian
let's say I would, I would have to

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:19.160
spend a lot of time speaking with
Iranians in, in Persian, in Farsi.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.880
Uh, but in this way that I work
with, with my tutor, I am building

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.560
up my potential, my capability.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.250
And I notice now that I understand
more than I did before, and

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:33.510
if I understand more, I will
eventually be able to speak better.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.690
I won't be able to remember all
the words, but I will gradually

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.190
be able to speak better.

00:06:39.015 --> 00:06:43.445
I have had this experience in
preparation for a trip to the Czech

00:06:43.785 --> 00:06:45.745
Republic, uh, Romania, Greece.

00:06:45.765 --> 00:06:49.635
I always step up by interaction
with my tutors to two or three times

00:06:49.635 --> 00:06:51.525
a week before going over there.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:56.535
And in fact, I sometimes try to
arrange for tutors, uh, as I did

00:06:56.565 --> 00:06:59.895
again with Ukrainian, interaction with
people while I'm over there, because

00:06:59.895 --> 00:07:05.135
it's sometimes difficult to, uh,
interact meaningfully with the locals.

00:07:05.594 --> 00:07:07.965
But I, in any case you
have to prepare for it.

00:07:08.115 --> 00:07:11.805
And that's why I think, depending on
your goals, it's worthwhile having a

00:07:11.805 --> 00:07:16.544
deliberate strategy in how you wanna
work with your online tutor, because

00:07:16.544 --> 00:07:20.055
it's a tremendous opportunity that
we have today, which didn't exist

00:07:20.325 --> 00:07:24.895
20 years ago to find people from the
country where the language is spoken.

00:07:25.975 --> 00:07:29.085
People who have different personalities,
so you can have more than one tutor,

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:35.400
and all of that helps keep your, you
know, largely in my case, input based

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.109
language, earning moving forward.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.320
So just some suggestions on
how to work with a tutor.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.750
And I'll leave you with a couple
of videos that I did on a similar

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.349
subject, uh, a while back, just
to see if my views have changed.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:47.729
Thank you for listening.

00:07:47.729 --> 00:07:48.300
By for now.

